    {
      "id": "p5cke72",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Neutralization Reaction"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t8hfpm3",
      "content": "Neutralization is the reaction between an acid and a base to form salt and water."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zs4oecn",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lrby5ha",
      "content": "HCl + NaOH → NaCl + H₂O"
    },
    {
      "id": "meff6br",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Salts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5d352hj",
      "content": "• Salts are ionic compounds formed from neutralization reactions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9fzm616",
      "content": "• They may be acidic, basic or neutral."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mf4fe1p",
      "content": "• Examples include sodium chloride, copper sulfate and ammonium chloride."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Litmus indicator is a natural dye extracted from lichens belonging to the division Thallophyta.",
        "Phenolphthalein indicator remains colorless in acidic solutions and turns bright pink in basic solutions.",
        "Plaster of Paris (CaSO4·1/2H2O) sets into hard Gypsum (CaSO4·2H2O) upon mixing with water.",
        "Milk of Magnesia [Mg(OH)2] is a mild base commonly used as an antacid to neutralize excess gastric acid."
      ],
      "id": "06d8am7"
    },
    {
      "id": "dkrtstw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. Uses of Acids, Bases and Salts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k1caozq",
      "content": "• Acids are used in batteries and fertilizers."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gf88jb7",
      "content": "• Bases are used in soap making and cleaning agents."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "no7fyjl",
      "content": "• Salts are used in food preservation and fertilizers."
    },
    {
      "id": "nwiax60",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "15yvr6e",
      "content": "• Acids produce hydrogen ions in water."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jrg8l0a",
      "content": "• Bases produce hydroxide ions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "y2ryi8v",
      "content": "• pH scale ranges from 0 to 14."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9ye4psd",
      "content": "• Neutralization produces salt and water."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}